## if/else in Rust
Rust's if/else looks familiar but with one key difference - **no parentheses** around the condition:
```rust
let x: i32 = 10;
if x > 5 {
    println!("Big");
} else {
    println!("Small");
}
```

Parentheses are optional but the compiler will warn you if you use them. Curly braces are always required.

